OL,3,A'Miracle' eagle with broken wing
OL,4,Aspotted back above Scottish coast
OL,5,
OL,6,FA sea eagle that confounded experts by
OL,7,Fsurviving into adulthood with a badly
OL,8,Fbroken wing has been spotted back in
OL,9,Fthe skies above Scotland's west coast.
OL,11,FThe bird was dubbed the Isle of Mull's
OL,12,F"miracle eagle" by charity the RSPB
OL,13,Fafter it fell from its nest as a chick
OL,14,Fduring a storm in 2023.
OL,16,FExperts that monitor the island's sea
OL,17,Feagle population did not expect the
OL,18,Fmale chick to survive, but it has now
OL,19,Fbeen spotted three years on - soaring
OL,20,Fabove the island with the distinctive
OL,21,Fkink in its wing clearly visible.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,308,300,200,140,0,100
